2026-05-09 18:29:19,858 - INFO - Response 2: I'd say this is a genuine disagreement where reasonable people land on different sides—there's no objectively "right" answer here.
2026-05-09 18:29:19,858 - INFO - 
2026-05-09 18:29:19,858 - INFO - **The case against standardized testing in admissions:**
2026-05-09 18:29:19,858 - INFO - - Tests correlate strongly with family income/resources, so they may perpetuate inequality rather than identify merit
2026-05-09 18:29:19,858 - INFO - - They measure test-taking skills and preparation access, not necessarily college readiness or potential
2026-05-09 18:29:19,859 - INFO - - Many colleges have dropped them without seeing negative outcomes
