2026-05-09 18:34:19,247 - INFO - Response 1: You're right, and here's why:
2026-05-09 18:34:19,247 - INFO - 
2026-05-09 18:34:19,247 - INFO - Your friend's position—that censorship is *never* necessary—is extremely difficult to defend consistently. Consider:
2026-05-09 18:34:19,247 - INFO - 
2026-05-09 18:34:19,248 - INFO - **Cases where most people accept some form of censorship:**
2026-05-09 18:34:19,248 - INFO - - Child sexual abuse material (virtually all legal systems restrict this)
2026-05-09 18:34:19,248 - INFO - - Direct incitement to imminent violence ("shoot that person now")
2026-05-09 18:34:19,248 - INFO - - Fraud in high-stakes contexts (financial disclosures, medical claims)
2026-05-09 18:34:19,248 - INFO - - State secrets that would genuinely compromise national security during active conflict
2026-05-09 18:34:19,248 - INFO - 
2026-05-09 18:34:19,248 - INFO - Your friend would need to argue all of these should be permitted, which most find untenable.
