2026-05-09 18:35:15,880 - INFO - - Whether current beauty standards are *too narrow* (they arguably are in most cultures)
2026-05-09 18:35:15,880 - INFO - - Whether the harms outweigh any benefits (evidence suggests they often do)
2026-05-09 18:35:15,880 - INFO - - Whether we can have aesthetic preferences without the toxic features of current standards (probably yes)
2026-05-09 18:35:15,880 - INFO - 
2026-05-09 18:35:15,880 - INFO - So rather than one person being right: the more accurate position is that beauty standards *as currently constructed and enforced* cause substantial harm that outweighs their benefits, even if some shared aesthetic frameworks might be harmless or even positive.
