2026-05-09 18:36:04,690 - INFO - **Why your friend has the stronger case:**
2026-05-09 18:36:04,690 - INFO - We have clear, lived evidence that our choices matter. You decide what to eat, whether to call someone, which job to pursue—and these decisions produce real consequences that differ from the alternative. If fate controlled everything, this wouldn't make sense: your deliberation would be illusory, and consequences would be identical regardless of your choice. They plainly aren't.
