2026-05-09 19:12:36,578 - INFO - - "Extreme longevity" remains speculative. We don't have working life-extension technologies yet—only incremental healthspan improvements. Treating this as an imminent threat inflates the urgency artificially.
2026-05-09 19:12:36,578 - INFO - - "Unprecedented inequality" is hyperbolic. Historical inequality in *access to basic medicine* (antibiotics, vaccines, surgery) already meant life-or-death disparities. That's not unprecedented.
2026-05-09 19:12:36,578 - INFO - - The "overpopulation" claim is debatable. Population growth is slowing globally; developed nations face aging/decline. Resource problems are typically about *distribution and consumption patterns*, not absolute scarcity.
